@*
    English counterpart of _SupportReport.tr.cshtml (App Store 1.2 — user generated content).
    No separate "In English" note here: the whole page is already English.
*@
<p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-5">
    What you save in Somine is your own private archive. A collection only becomes visible to
    anyone else when its owner shares it with a specific person, or creates a public link for it.
    Even so, if you come across insults, harassment, hate speech, sexual content, copyright
    infringement or anything unlawful in a collection shared with you — or behind a public
    Somine link — we want you to tell us.
</p>

<div class="rounded-xl bg-white border border-[#E8F1EF] p-5 mb-5">
    <p class="font-medium text-gray-800 text-sm mb-2">Report it in the app (fastest)</p>
    <ol class="text-gray-500 text-sm space-y-1 list-decimal pl-5">
        <li>Open the collection that was shared with you, or find it under <em>Shared With Me</em>.</li>
        <li>Tap the <span class="font-medium text-gray-700">&quot;…&quot;</span> button in the top right.</li>
        <li>Choose <span class="font-medium text-gray-700">Report collection</span> and pick a reason.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm mt-3">
        From the same menu you can <span class="font-medium text-gray-700">block</span> the person, or leave
        the share by choosing <span class="font-medium text-gray-700">Remove from my library</span>.
        Reports are confidential: the person you report never sees who reported them.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="rounded-xl bg-white border border-[#E8F1EF] p-5 mb-5">
    <p class="font-medium text-gray-800 text-sm mb-2">Reporting a public link (somineapp.com/s/…) or without an account</p>
    <a href="mailto:abuse@somineapp.com?subject=Content%20report%20—%20Somine"
       class="text-[#688E8B] font-medium hover:underline">
        abuse@somineapp.com
    </a>
    <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm mt-3 mb-1">Include these details and we can resolve it faster:</p>
    <ul class="text-gray-500 text-sm space-y-1 list-disc pl-5">
        <li>The link to the page you are reporting (<span class="font-mono text-xs">somineapp.com/s/…</span>) or the name of the collection</li>
        <li>The username of the person who shared it</li>
        <li>What the problem is, and a screenshot if you have one</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-5">
    <span class="font-medium text-gray-800">What we do:</span> reports reach our moderator by email
    straight away and are reviewed <span class="font-medium text-gray-800">within 24 hours</span>. Where a
    violation is confirmed, we take the content down, disable the public link, and suspend or close the
    account if the violation is serious or repeated. If you reported by email, we write back with the outcome.
</p>

<p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-5">
    <span class="font-medium text-gray-800">Protecting yourself:</span> turn down a share request from
    someone you don&apos;t know with <span class="font-medium text-gray-800">Decline and block</span>. Once
    blocked, they can&apos;t send you collections, anything they shared with you leaves your library, and
    they aren&apos;t notified. You can see and unblock people from the <em>Shared With Me</em> screen. You can
    also revoke any public link you created, at any time.
</p>
